    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter July 3rd with a clear offensive blueprint, anchored by the elite tier of **Yordan Alvarez** (82.21) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our primary catalyst against Nick Martinez, benefiting from an elite 0.477 xwOBA and favorable platoon alignment that juices his score. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-priority start in the leadoff spot; his combination of top-of-the-order usage and the matchup against Pallante creates a perfect storm for stolen base production, a category we are prioritizing aggressively to close the gap in the 5x5 standings. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong 75.84 rating as he\u2019s projected into the leadoff role against Jose Cabrera, where his dynamic platoon advantage and current form make him a must-start despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status.\n\nOur middle infield strategy shifts today toward **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Junior Caminero** (72.33), both of whom are poised to exploit advantageous matchups. **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a solid 0.379 xwOBA, while **Casey Schmitt** sees his value inflated by an impressive 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a prime #2 spot in the order. On the bench, **Luke Raley** (38.17) served as the primary alternative but was ultimately relegated due to the looming threat of Dylan Cease\u2019s arm, which suppressed his efficiency score below our 40.0 baseline. We are monitoring **Chase Meidroth** (36.56) closely as well, though a 38% rain probability and a difficult matchup against Williams keep him firmly on the pine as we prioritize the higher-floor profiles of **Carson Benge** (63.98) and **Nelson Velazquez** (58.20) to maintain our game cap integrity.",
